{"title":"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is called solitary if, for any nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e42302f9dd0afe4a7cd50ac2115f72bee849423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> contains the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when written in base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Determine, with proof, the number of solitary integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/042b44ed762ce8a071b63c5b94d3adccd573ded3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{2026}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Lemma 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27cd0fb3685a62d6adf0053967ad7b8e242dad2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2\\cdot 10^k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"19\" /> is solitary for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a158c5dc4263f35c85831000776100070d62c23d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\geq 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" />.</b>\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e42302f9dd0afe4a7cd50ac2115f72bee849423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. WLOG, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d997b30f7f09d32954c9b09f04a6599729dd6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/733993fb4ce7b4951cb0785a898a690e298f4871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a\\geq a+b=n\\implies a \\geq \\frac{n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"218\" height=\"34\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/375398566c85556f748c4d7587b522ceffcdb1b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" /> are integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, this implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d722bfce16d3ac029cdb29d60144fffa758e99b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\geq \\frac{n+1}{2}=10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />. But, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98e34f38bc1f3da434a01f4503a9eb7f11c7cd16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\leq n = 2\\cdot 10^k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d303caca61913050dcac25b6a79b700ed9e2c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^k \\leq a \\leq 2\\cdot 10^k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />, so the leading digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is solitary. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Lemma 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e580f39032aa9260c0cf830fcb785bba5fc98445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2\\cdot 10^k+n, n &lt; 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"21\" /> is solitary if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is solitary.</b>\n</p><p>First, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is solitary and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not. We write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa8d1552c6bba160defacbe7b1ae9c0252c79e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> with no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s in their decimal representation. Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a7c0e125238109569b4b5b3f31e516518f766f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39; = a +2\\cdot 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56fc8c06f0d50713d72b66c017eb13ca84e5767b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39; = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c1be0acdecb940fcf5f6f3b2d1b6468645fafb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a&#39;+b&#39; = a+2\\cdot 10^k+b=2\\cdot 10^k+n=m\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"17\" />\nBut <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1e51ef5511c6d27c703b84edc8ff93ffbc3717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;$\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> have no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s in their decimal representation, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a55a272ee64cf76d6e70cf01c0307df9e0ff817b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^k &gt; n \\geq a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" />, a contradiction. This proves the only if part.\n</p><p><br />\nNow, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is solitary, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is not. Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac0a93ba6f5f8aa9bc4cbdaaf73b0057c5f969c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> with no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s in their decimal representation.\n</p><p>Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bbadb9c1020b6c737691213a02b07ac8b22f598.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = x\\cdot 10^k+a&#39;, a&#39;&lt; 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"21\" /> (the leading digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />). Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a90bdc55136982ae4b4c4bb33e7dd659d3d2d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = y\\cdot 10^k+b&#39;, b&#39;&lt; 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"21\" />. By definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06a110024c14495c28a6b88d67283e4abaf1cd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b \\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/70076ce837f4f6c13fb01efbacd0c83883e62450.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=y=0\\implies a+b&lt; 2\\cdot 10^k &lt; n \\text{ and } x + y &gt; 2\\implies a+b\\geq 3\\cdot 10^k &gt; m\\]\" width=\"548\" height=\"19\" /> Thus, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the other is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6edda12e4271ad04f65fe197a8d4cd225cacf338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2, y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"17\" />. Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1e51ef5511c6d27c703b84edc8ff93ffbc3717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;$\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e43202b1701c00329db42e0e666bd1210c10ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a&#39;+b&#39; = m- x\\cdot 10^k -y\\cdot 10^k =m - 2\\cdot 10^k = n\\]\" width=\"378\" height=\"19\" /> But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is solitary, so either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1e51ef5511c6d27c703b84edc8ff93ffbc3717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;$\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39574adf537bc19e989f7b69bee4bf19c7d7f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in their decimal representation. But, that implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> also has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25aaaa7e67a7cebfa5d1998dabd1eb4ba3ad1098.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;, b&#39; &lt; 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"21\" />, a contradiction. This proves the if part. The lemma is complete. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Lemma 3: For any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd181d547fb8d0fae6890e011785c447867a07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in [10^k, 10^{k+1}-1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"22\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is not of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/053af3d1318fc09e3e99ab90628f4319ee729b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 10^k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"19\" /> and not of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e4f6aaced0c1a6196881445438fc84d5d935b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 10^k + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1ccba24a352cb43ae5b7d5bc4eb20928fb573ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />), then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is not solitary.</b>\n</p><p>By Lemma 2, we can assume the leading digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now, take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0dc8267006d16afa843f6e5b60993862469118c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=10^k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/629e675818959e2c05bc7273b2db2e203ba04136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = m-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Let the decimal representations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb7a77a22d53ce5a1246c2b262d093782475bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-1}a_{k-2}\\dots a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4b9ce43ec097a7212001c0c549d01094ef3197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_kb_{k-1}\\dots b_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c129213d28dd1afb9f19c0fe98e2c82a03a73b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5ea0453284ed26397eeef6ddc00d885f97db6f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\notin [2\\cdot 10^k-1, 3\\cdot 10^k-1]\\implies b = m-a \\notin [10^k, 2\\cdot 10^k]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"463\" height=\"22\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b174991ab2ab6900080911cde9454f3a7902868e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k\\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nNow, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b19bebefa50621e43cfd88e4f24dbf8d126195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i = 1, i\\in \\{0, 1, \\dots, k-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" />. Increase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and lower <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This increases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a605afcc5b95a9a80915af1218cd379415674e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> while decreasing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a605afcc5b95a9a80915af1218cd379415674e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />, so the sum stays the same. Repeating this for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d599dc5535d13ff701f42e739a9a4ba40a00763.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> such that none of the digits are 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a157b3c565d610af1337dd8f7d3d1021fa5d2fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is not solitary. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNow, we use the lemmas to finish. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc028050428615cc28ee3c1f9a67eda8e9a726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of solitary integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5cf3b363ac770e73ca25a3ef982e73058c4c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt; 10^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e880b118bfa7c5db071a4ed8bb0890168702843f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> be the set of these integers, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/3/15386879d390d6a4f2adde3bf026b2f8ca9b54d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_k|=s_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. By the lemmas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39f6b48f2f98b238361427a5f30a0fdae6df203.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_{k+1} = \\{2\\cdot 10^k-1\\} \\cup \\{2\\cdot 10^k+n : n\\in S_k \\}\\cup S_k\\]\" width=\"384\" height=\"20\" /> Since no elements are shared, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6459fa5819da855027440d4dff6dac18a4955527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{k+1} = 1 + s_k+s_k=2s_k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/6020272a4e4ead4ad748e7416ded1b7286ff3e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1 = \\{1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b1ad0fbf026147b1936e9c69c8a3f6d5282351a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. It follows by induction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8fac460fa48c1432bf055cde637b776687c42c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k = 2^k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c29e0674a8c5d389ac88af6c7e07ec4d6c88d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2^{2026}-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"81\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~sillybone\n</p><p>~Lemma 3 by Hpenguin\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Lemma 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must contain 1, otherwise it is not solitary.\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma 1:</b>\n</p><p>Definition of solitary, choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7e6cff29278d6a6f3b7d694b12640f11b046fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and the result shows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not solitary.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2:</b>: All such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has the property all digits to the right of \"1\" are \"9\".\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma 2:</b>\n</p><p>Consider vertical addition. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th place value of such numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/2600eb5ddef38276ed37d9d6b4a22f4d40dbb51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 + b_0 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />. One can form such numbers using any orientation, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/559d5d5764d45ded08233db4c6e2db387af2ee84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d43962bde5fd7992cbf1f482a15d56af2f3e3002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, vice versa, or some non-1 pair. Assume the worst case, where we construct sums of 9 that do not include 1. Then, if the leading digit itself is 1, then notice that one may \"truncate\" the 19 at the end of the string <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f17d52404a786eace5f24cddb3b9096d0e490a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1999\\dots 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />. Because 9 is solitary, any single combination of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a37bbf011fce8765b98bd83ef191b6184f3eecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> result in one value being greater than 10, hence we must carry a value. Specifically, that implies the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> or vice versa. Hence, if the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is obtained, then notice that then one can let, at the end of the truncation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> start with 9 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> begin with 10, giving the 19 that was truncated at the beginning. This fulfills solitary properties.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 3:</b> All such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has the property all digits to the left of \"1\" are either \"0\" or \"2\" or a combination of both.\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma 3:</b>\n</p><p>We continue from where we left off in Lemma 2. We realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must start with a 0 then move through with 9's. Afterwards, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are uniquely determined toward the left side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />'s 1 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />'s 0. Consider forming a sum of 11 instead of 1, and we prove that a number can be formed that is solitary. More importantly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> do not contain 1 at all yet still sum to 11, then that 1 carries over. Now, we still fulfill the properties of <b>Lemma 2</b>, but the number is not solitary! But if we were to carry over that extra 1, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cfb07e4911e7b4f994b858f3d47604ddbee438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aedf59c6a301c8af3ee1244a2c75fcc993349fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> can have either 1 or 9, from which we terminate, or continue analogously. However, when we end, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> has 1, hence the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is solitary.\n</p><p><b>2026 USAMO/Q4:</b>\n</p><p>Given the conditions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <i>solitary</i> if and only if\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> contains 1</li></ul>\n<ul><li>All numbers to the right of the 1 in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are 9</li></ul>\n<ul><li>All numbers to the left of the 1 in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are \"2\" or \"0\"</li></ul>\n<p>The last part is to count all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. From any number, the digit 1 can be placed at an index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> from the left (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748003791ff2db23f21b69a357d4e21ce74d6c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq m \\leq 2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />). \n</p><p>There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e01ea65f81ef9f88094ee65d968ab3119385bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026 - m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> positions to the right of 1 that are all 9. Otherwise, there are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96eec32de93b032b6d531a03aa5b346156b62a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> positions to the left of 1. Those have two choices each, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706502b1171e45f0cb6b7283791098c36378acea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> cases. So, on any given integer with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> digits, we may form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706502b1171e45f0cb6b7283791098c36378acea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> solitary integers.\n</p><p>We sum over all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748003791ff2db23f21b69a357d4e21ce74d6c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq m \\leq 2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />, or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/3900bfaf1afb1d7d87ca9442f24d273b02ca9d71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m = 1}^{2026} 2^{m-1} = 1+2+\\dots+2^{2025} = \\boxed{2^{2026}-1} \\quad \\square\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO\" title=\"2026 USAMO\">2026 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172751\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.054 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.073 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 811/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27185/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.286      1 -total\n 58.55%    7.193      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 39.69%    4.876      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36114:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172751 and revision id 287558. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}